$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: smith-gray/control-plane
$type: service
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-09-22"
summary: |
  Control Plane API — issues and revokes capability tokens, manages policy, and exposes the audit log. It never receives plaintext secrets. Built in Go on Postgres, authenticating sidecars and CLIs via API key in the MVP and mTLS later.

$system: smith-gray/system
name: Control Plane API
status: planned
type: api
runtime: go
port: 8080
paths:
  - apps/control-plane
depends_on:
  - key-store
  - postgres

tech_stack:
  language: Go
  framework: net/http (standard library) or chi
  database: Postgres
  key_store: OpenBao or Vault (Transit / KV)
  migrations: SQL migrations applied at boot
  observability: Prometheus metrics and structured logs

dev:
  command: "go run ./apps/control-plane/cmd/server"
  url: "http://localhost:8080"
  env:
    DATABASE_URL: postgres://localhost:5432/safekeys
    KEYSTORE_ADDR: http://localhost:8200
    KEYSTORE_TOKEN: dev-only-token
    CONTROL_PLANE_API_KEY: dev-only-api-key

prod:
  url: ""
  region: ""
  deployment_ref: ""

testing:
  framework: Go testing + testcontainers for Postgres
  command: "go test ./apps/control-plane/..."
  coverage_target: "80%"

security:
  auth_method: API key (MVP), mutual TLS for sidecars (later)
  secrets_ref: docs/help/control-plane-auth.md

rbac:
  description: |
    Two client classes in the MVP. Human operators hold admin credentials (create/revoke policy,
    read audit). Sidecars hold narrow credentials scoped to their environment and may only request
    unwrap and report resolves.
  roles:
    - name: operator
      level: admin
    - name: sidecar
      level: resolve-only
    - name: auditor
      level: read-only

modules:
  - name: api
    purpose: HTTP handlers for token issue, revoke, policy, and audit endpoints
    paths: [apps/control-plane/internal/api]
  - name: token
    purpose: Capability token minting, signing (kid), TTL and scope validation, jti registry
    paths: [apps/control-plane/internal/token]
  - name: policy
    purpose: Policy evaluation — which sidecar may resolve which object for which scope
    paths: [apps/control-plane/internal/policy]
  - name: audit
    purpose: Append-only audit records for create, resolve, deny, and revoke events
    paths: [apps/control-plane/internal/audit]
  - name: keystore
    purpose: Client for OpenBao/Vault — envelope key wrapping and unwrap brokering
    paths: [apps/control-plane/internal/keystore]

risks:
  - "Control plane credential compromise could mint tokens — mitigated because the plane holds no plaintext and the master key lives in the key store or hardware element."
  - "Postgres is a single point of failure for policy and audit; MVP accepts this with backups."

future:
  - "Multi-tenant hosted authority with SSO and compliance reporting."
  - "mTLS device identity binding for sidecars."

decisions:
  - id: go-and-postgres
    decision: Implement the control plane in Go backed by Postgres.
    rationale: Go gives a single static binary for operators, a strong standard library for HTTP and crypto, and shares a toolchain with the CLI and sidecar. Postgres provides transactional policy and audit storage.
    status: accepted
  - id: no-plaintext-at-control-plane
    decision: The control plane must never accept or store plaintext secret material.
    rationale: Keeps the most network-exposed component outside the decryption path, so its compromise alone cannot reveal secrets.
    status: accepted
